=== tests/fm-wake-drain-outcome-backstop.test.sh ===
ok - a newest keyless done, blocked, or needs-decision event with no newer branch outcome surfaces on the next main drain
ok - a newer task-matching branch outcome suppresses the backstop and routine latest events stay silent
ok - only a strictly newer outcome for the same task can suppress its latest captain event
ok - a branch annotation and queue acknowledgement cannot consume the main drain's loss backstop
ok - status byte position distinguishes handled and later same-second events
ok - drain cost and suppression are independent of append-only outcome history
ok - backstop receipts prevent repeats without consuming delayed signal annotations
ok - a failed output consumer leaves the backstop unacknowledged for retry
ok - receipt failure may repeat a presented backstop but cannot lose it
ok - captain-facing decisions rejected by the fold surface once
ok - a missing outcome index self-heals on the first drain and suppresses its handled status
ok - a fresh home with a status log and no index surfaces the backstop on its first drain
ok - a genuine outcome-store fault fails closed without Pi-specific restart advice
ok - held-lock initialization rejects callers outside the lock owner's process tree
ok - held-lock initialization accepts a descendant of the outcome lock owner
ok - index self-heal runs only while the outcome lock is held
ok - an over-bound unclassifiable routine event stays silent
ok - a latest-event append is deferred and its final completion surfaces on retry
ok - the outcome backstop caps each item and its total task output deterministically

